<title>POLAND: Polifarb-C workers on strike alert.</title>
<headline>Polifarb-C workers on strike alert.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish paint marker Polifarb Cieszyn SA said on Wednesday that its employees went on strike alert because of concerns over a planned merger with Polifarb Wroclaw later this year.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that Polifarb-Cieszyn's board did not share the trade unions' worries about moving the firm's headquarters to Wroclaw and changing the firm's name.</p>
<p>Under the merger plan Cieszyn would raise its share capital by 2,978,820 shares to equal Wroclaw's 22,103,820 shares.</p>
<p>Later Cieszyn would set another issue for Wroclaw shareholders and a one-for-one share exchange would take place to effect the merger.</p>
<p>Analysts said the two firms would command about 40 percent of Poland's paint market after the consolidation.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
